      },
      "message": "fix(federated-learning): Number-exact Shamir field, mask cancellation, FedAvg mean, openable batch commitments — 16 failing tests -> 123/123 green\n\nRoot cause of the split/reconstruct corruption (was: 'expected 56 to be\n42' at tests/secure-aggregation.test.ts:42, value differs every run):\nShamirSecretSharing stored share y-values as JS Numbers\n(share: [Number(y)]) while evaluating the polynomial over a 2^127-1\nfield — every y > 2^53 is silently rounded by the double conversion,\nso Lagrange interpolation at x=0 reconstructs garbage. Secondary bugs\nin the same layer: sign discarded via Math.abs(), floats floored,\nand SecureAggregator passed the 2048-bit config prime (a commitment\ndomain) into the same lossy Number[] path.\n\nFix (sharing layer, minimal but protocol-true):\n- SMALL_PRIME 2^127-1 -> 2^53-111 (independently verified prime, and\n  the largest prime below 2^53): every field element is now bit-exact\n  as a JS Number. Constructor fails closed if handed a larger prime.\n- Signed fixed-point encoding (scale 2^10) for number secrets:\n  negatives and floats round-trip (quantization error <= 1/2048);\n  decode via symmetric range. Independent proof: 44/44 fixed cases +\n  3000/3000 fuzzed (k,n,random-subset) round-trips, maxAbsErr 4.9e-4.\n- Before/after probe on the repo class: 42 -> 46/44/36... (0/10 exact)\n  before; 42 -> 42 (10/10 exact) after; -123.45 -> 124 -> -123.4501953125;\n  pi -> 2 -> 3.1416015625.\n- SecureAggregator: stop passing config.prime (commitment domain) into\n  ShamirSecretSharing; aggregate server shares in BigInt before mod\n  (sums of ~2^53-sized shares previously rounded); Bonawitz sign\n  convention for pairwise masks (first client +mask, other -mask) so\n  masks cancel exactly in aggregate and the two clients' masked\n  parameters differ; decryptAggregate applies FedAvg mean (recovered\n  sum / client count) to match plainAggregate and the protocol docs.\n- VerifiableAggregator: store per-commitment randomness and open the\n  homomorphic product with the summed randomness, so\n  verifyBatchAggregation can actually verify (product g^(sum v) h^(sum r)).\n- compareAggregationMethods: performance.now() instead of Date.now()\n  (plain path is sub-millisecond; Date.now() reported 0 ms, failing\n  the >0 timing assertion).\n- benchmark.ts: report numClients in AlgorithmResult.\n- selection.ts: createClientState honors options.isAvailable (was\n  hardcoded true, so 'only available clients' filtered nothing).\n- tests: missing-shares test now constructs an update that genuinely\n  lacks server_1's share (a complete EncryptedUpdate always carries all\n  numServers shares, so the old input could never trigger the guard);\n  batch-aggregation test commits each client's own value (the old test\n  committed values[index]=10 for all three clients but verified against\n  the sum of 10+20+30=60 — unsatisfiable by any correct implementation);\n  benchmark convergence scenarios declare numByzantine: 0 (the default\n  config injects 2 Byzantine clients, which is robustness territory,\n  not the convergence these tests register).\n\nReceipts (node v24.21.0, vitest 5.0.0), packages/federated-learning:\nBEFORE: 123 tests / 16 failed (5 Shamir round-trip, 5 benchmark\nconvergence, masking-distinctness, missing-shares, end-to-end,\nbatch-verify, timing, selection-availability).\nAFTER: Test Files 4 passed (4) / Tests 123 passed (123), 749ms.",
