      "message": "fix: resolve install ERESOLVE — align vitest/coverage-v8/@types/node peers; point test:unit & test:e2e at real dirs\n\n- @vitest/coverage-v8 ^4.1.7 -> ^5.0.0: coverage-v8 5.x peer vitest 5.0.x\n  matches root vitest ^5.0.0; the 4.x pin (peer vitest 4.1.11) made\n  npm install / npm ci fail with ERESOLVE on a fresh clone.\n- @types/node ^20.19.43 -> ^22.20.4: vitest@5.0.0 declares peerOptional\n  @types/node ^22.0.0 || >=24.0.0 (vite 8.3.0 wants ^20.19.0 || >=22.12.0);\n  ^22.20.4 satisfies both — required for vitest 5 to install.\n- test:unit/test:e2e pointed at tests/unit and tests/e2e, which do not\n  exist ('No test files found', exit 1). Real locations: unit tests live\n  under packages/*/ (integration package excluded), e2e/integration tests\n  live in packages/integration-tests (50 test files, exists).\n\nVerified: fresh 'npm install' resolves cleanly (vitest 5.0.0 +\n@vitest/coverage-v8 5.0.0 + @types/node 22.20.4, 0 vulnerabilities);\n'npm run test:e2e' discovers and runs 206 integration tests.",
